      <div type="clause" n="3">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Blas">Blas</ref> 3</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="3" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="388" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif he ðone að forþbringan ne mæg ⁊ he þonne fúl sy, stande on þæra yldesta manna dome, hweþer he lif áge þe nage, þe to ðære byrig hyran.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="†" target="#Blas_3.lnote.oe.dagger"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="3" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="388" ed="#liebermann"/>Gyf he ðonne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Blas_3.lnote.oe.6"/> að forðbringan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Blas_3.lnote.oe.7"/> ne mæge ⁊ he ðonne ful sy, stonde on ðara yldestana manna dome, hwæðer he hlif<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Blas_3.lnote.oe.8"/> ag<hi rend="italic">e</hi> ðe nág<hi rend="italic">e</hi>, þe to ðære byrig hyron<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Blas_3.lnote.oe.9"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="3" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="389" ed="#liebermann"/>Si iusiurandum perficere<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Blas_3.lnote.oe.3"/> nequeat, ut reus (non direxerit et<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Blas_3.lnote.oe.10"/> culpabilis) sit, stet in seniorum hominum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Blas_3.lnote.oe.11"/> iudicio, utrum uitam habeat uel<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Blas_3.lnote.oe.12"/> non habeat, qui ad ipsam curiam obediunt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Blas_3.lnote.oe.13"/> (pertinent)<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#Blas_3.lnote.oe.14"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="3" corresp="#wit-cons"><pb n="389" ed="#liebermann"/>Si iuramentum illi deficit, qui si ceciderit, in decreto seniorum sit, qui ad illam urbem attinent, utrum uita ei concedatur, an morte puniatur.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-h">Gif he þone að forðbringan ne mæg, and he þonne fúl sy, stande on þæra yldesta<ptr type="editorNote" n="4" target="#Blas_3.attnote.fn.4"/> manna dome, hweðer he lif áge þe nage, þe to þære byrig hyran.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="389" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn jener solchen Eid nicht zu Stande zu bringen vermag, und er also schuldig dasteht, so stehe es in der Entscheidung der angesehensten<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Blas_3.lnote.de.1"/> Männer<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Blas_3.lnote.de.2"/>, die zu jener Gerichtsstätte gehören, ob er das Leben<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Blas_3.lnote.de.3"/> behalte oder verliere<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Blas_3.lnote.de.4"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If he cannot bring forward such an oath, and he thus stands guilty, let it rest with the judgment of the most senior men who belong to that place of court [borough] whether he keeps his life or loses it.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-h">If he [the accused] cannot produce the oath<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#Blas_3.attnote.n.2"/> and is proved guilty, the chief men of the borough shall decide whether his life shall be spared or not.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#wormald" corresp="#wit-h">If he cannot produce the oath and so be guilty, let it be in the judgement of the most senior men that belong to the borough whether he have life or not.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="389"><ref target="clause:IIAs_20-1">II As 20.1</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">II As. 20, 1</note>
        <note type="editorial">In all MSS Forfang follows without a break, perhaps taken from the same royal law. With ‘bringan’ a new quire begins in B, which was mistakenly bound at the front (now p. 1). Liebermann compares II As 20.1.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 388, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Blas_3.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">388</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vgl. I Cn.</hi> 6, 1 <hi rend="italic">A</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cf. I Cn. 6, 1 A</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Blas_3.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">388</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">mit</hi> bringan <hi rend="italic">beginnt neue Lage, die irrthümlich zu vorderst gebunden ist, also p.</hi> 1</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">with bringan a new quire begins, which has been bound in first by mistake, hence p. 1</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Blas_3.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">388</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vgl.</hi> gehleafan <hi rend="italic">I Cn.</hi> 22, 1</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cf. gehleafan I Cn. 22, 1</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Blas_3.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">388</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">in ders. Zeile folgt</hi> Forfang.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">in the same line there follows Forfang.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Blas_3.lnote.oe.dagger" n="†" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">388</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Ohne Absatz folgt in allen Hss., vielleicht demselben Königsgesetz entnommen:</hi> Forfang.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Without a paragraph break there follows in all MSS, perhaps taken from the same royal law: Forfang.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Blas_3.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">389</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">in <hi rend="italic">geänd.</hi> ab <hi rend="italic">Co;</hi> ab <hi rend="italic">OrRMHk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">in altered to ab Co; ab OrRMHk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Blas_3.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">389</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">forf. <hi rend="italic">MHk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">forf. MHk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Blas_3.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">389</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">de <hi rend="italic">fügt zu Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">de added by Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Blas_3.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">389</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">u. a. <hi rend="italic">fehlt K, am Rande Co</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">u. a. missing in K, in the margin in Co</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Blas_3.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">389</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">antip. <hi rend="italic">R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">antip. R</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Blas_3.lnote.oe.14" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">389</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">folgt</hi> Forfang.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">followed by Forfang.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Blas_3.lnote.oe.star2" n="**" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">389</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">bessere</hi> et</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">read et</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Blas_3.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">389</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">incidit <hi rend="italic">statt</hi> si c. <hi rend="italic">Hr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">incidit instead of si c. Hr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Blas_3.lnote.oe.6-2" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">389</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ei u. <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ei u. Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Blas_3.lnote.oe.7-2" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">389</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">folgt</hi> Forfang.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">followed by Forfang.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Blas_3.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">229</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">ful wære</hi> II As 5.—Über die Genetivendung <hi rend="italic">-sta</hi>, <hi rend="italic">-stana</hi> <hi rend="italic">s</hi>. Sievers <hi rend="italic">Gramm</hi>. § 304 A. 2</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">ful wære</hi> II As 5.—On the genitive ending <hi rend="italic">-sta</hi>, <hi rend="italic">-stana</hi> <hi rend="italic">see</hi> Sievers <hi rend="italic">Gramm</hi>. § 304 n. 2</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Blas_3.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">229</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Urteilfinder 2k. l</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Urteilfinder 2k. l</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Blas_3.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">229</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Wörtlich wie Ine 6 = Grið 9</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Word for word as Ine 6 = Grið 9</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Blas_3.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">229</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Brandstiftung 2. 3. 4a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Brandstiftung 2. 3. 4a</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Blas_3.attnote.n.2" n="2" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">173</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">cf. I Edw 3; II As. 6.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Blas_3.attnote.fn.4" n="4" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">170</biblScope></bibl><label>yldesta</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">yldestana.</hi> B.</seg></note>
